2:T5b5,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get my money back from an investment scam?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Recovery of investment scam losses is very difficult — typically under 10% of victims recover funds. You should immediately report to the FMA and NZ Police, and contact your bank to attempt to trace or reverse any transfers. If funds went overseas, recovery becomes even harder. Acting within the first 24-48 hours gives the best chance of a bank recall."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I check if an investment is legitimate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Check the FMA's Financial Service Providers Register (FSPR) at fspr.govt.nz to verify the firm is licensed. Check the FMA's warning list for known scams. Search for reviews and complaints. Ask for a Product Disclosure Statement (PDS) — all regulated investment offers require one. If any of these checks fail, don't invest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a \"pig butchering\" scam?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pig butchering is a sophisticated scam where criminals spend weeks or months building a romantic or friendly relationship with the victim online before introducing an \"investment opportunity.\" Once the victim has \"invested\" significant funds (been \"fattened up\"), the criminals take all the money and disappear. These scams are now extremely common."}}]}6:["slug","investment-scams","d"]
